 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Save the dates go out roughly six months before the wedding. It gives people enough time to plan to come. August is right on the edge. It depends how far away the venue is and whether there flights getting in that time. Email is fine as long as it goes with a printed reminder a few weeks before. Most people check both. That's the right spirit. Just make sure the paper is thick and the date is easy to read. The invites can be simple and straightforward. Just remember to include a little about the wedding date, time and venue.",
